BFIN_MEM_STALL=1: what the GUI core waits for memory, as a first-order model (cache misses and uncached SDRAM accesses).

Off by default; with it, dv-bfin_mmu.c classifies every load, store and instruction fetch by the CPLBs and a 16 KB I-cache / 16-32 KB D-cache, and the cycles go to the instruction that waited (the virtual time base advances by them).  BFIN_STALL_FILL / _RD / _WR / _ASYNC / _MMR set the costs; BFIN_STATS adds a "STATS mem" line with the counters.

